      "message": "test(mcp): the posts folder test uses native absolute paths\n\nOn Windows a path needs its drive to be absolute, so \"/p/posts\" and\n\"/h\" read as relative there and the folder test failed. The test now\nuses drive-qualified paths on Windows and Unix paths elsewhere, builds\nthe expected folders with PathBuf::join, and adds the XDG_DATA_HOME and\nAPPDATA cases.\n\nRefs #2074\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
